  address = {Baku, Azerbaijan},
  abstract = {At present, the issue of sending humans to a lunar orbit and landing on the surface is being considered. One of the main ways to deliver a crew to the Moon is a direct flight to a low lunar orbit, similar to the Apollo program. NASA proposes Gateway Program: deploying a lunar orbital station in a Near-Rectilinear Halo Orbit (NRHO) that would be used as a Spaceport for deep-space missions. As an alternative idea of the Spaceport, it is proposed to deploy the orbital station in a circular polar High Lunar Orbit (HLO) with an altitude of 10, 000 km. This paper proposes a Gravispheric transfer method to HLO using an intermediate orbit with an apoapsis in the vicinity of the Moon's gravispheric boundary. Calculations show that the Gravispheric transfer allows reaching HLO with lower delta-V budget compared to the direct HLO transfer or NRHO insertion. The paper describes a transportation system to deliver the crew to the South Pole of the Moon with the use of the Gravispheric transfer to the Lunar orbital station in HLO.},
