  abstract = {This paper presents the design and implementation of a model predictive control (MPC) system to guide and control a chasing spacecraft during rendezvous with a passive target spacecraft in an elliptical or circular orbit, from the point of target detection all the way to capture. To achieve an efficient system design, the rendezvous man\oe uvre has been partitioned into three main phases based on the range of operation, plus a collision-avoidance man\oe uvre to be used in event of a fault. Each has its own associated MPC controller. Linear time varying models are used to enable trajectory predictions in elliptical orbits, whilst a variable prediction horizon is used to achieve finite-time completion of man\oe uvres, and a 1-norm cost on velocity change minimises propellant consumption. Constraints are imposed to ensure that trajectories do not collide with the target. A key feature of the design is the implementation of non-convex constraints as switched convex constraints, enabling the use of convex linear and quadratic programming. The system is implemented using commercial-off-the-shelf tools with deployment through the use of automatic code generation in mind, and validated by closed-loop simulation. A significant reduction in total propellant consumption in comparison with a baseline benchmark solution is observed.},
  langid = {english},
  annotation = {titleTranslation: 航天器交会模型预测控制系统设计与实现\\
abstractTranslation: 本文提出了一种模型预测控制（MPC）系统的设计与实现，用于引导和控制追踪航天器在椭圆或圆轨道上与被动目标航天器进行交会，涵盖从目标探测直至捕获的全过程。为实现高效系统设计，交会机动根据操作距离划分为三个主要阶段，并附加一个用于故障情况下的避碰机动。每个阶段均配备相应的MPC控制器。采用线性时变模型实现椭圆轨道中的轨迹预测，同时利用可变预测时域实现机动的有限时间完成，并以速度变化的1-范数代价最小化推进剂消耗。施加约束以确保轨迹不与目标发生碰撞。该设计的一个关键特征是将非凸约束实现为切换凸约束，从而能够使用凸线性规划和二次规划。系统采用商用现成工具实现，并考虑通过自动代码生成进行部署，通过闭环仿真进行验证。与基线基准方案相比，总推进剂消耗显著降低。},
  file = {/home/ouyangjiahong/Zotero/storage/DE2LU7PM/Hartley 等 - 2012 - Model predictive control system design and implementation for spacecraft rendezvous.pdf}
}

