  abstract = {The primary objective of this study is to design low energy transfer orbits to Near Rectilinear Halo Orbit around the Lagrange Point-2 of the Earth-Moon system, which is the potential location of future deep-space gateway. The deep-space gateway concept is being discussed and studied in the international space community for future Lunar and deep-space exploration including Human Mars exploration. When considering the transportation of the cargo between Earth and the gateway, there are several methods for the transfer. Among the methods, especially the low-energy transfer will be a strong candidate for the cargo missions due to the low delta-V required. To construct the strategy of the low-energy transfer orbit design, this study adopts Parker's method to design the transfer orbits to Near Rectilinear Halo Orbit. Not only to design the low-energy NRHO transfer orbit, this study also focuses on the reduction of the Time-of-Flight for the transfer by applying Deep Space Maneuvers.},
