  doi = {10.1016/j.asr.2018.10.026},
  urldate = {2025-11-20},
  abstract = {An analytical expression for distant retrograde orbits (DROs) is obtained in this study. Owing to the fact that a planar DRO is a closed orbit and can be expressed as an approximately elliptical orbit, respective geometries and periods of DROs are analytically calculated. A switching point, where various properties of planar DROs change abruptly with an increase in the orbital radius, is determined. The Mars--Deimos system is taken as a case study in this work. The proposed method can be applied to cases where the Hill's approximation of the restricted three-body problem is valid. Numerical calculations are performed to validate the proposed method.},
  langid = {english},
  keywords = {Analytical solution,Distant retrograde orbit,Hill three-body problem,Small natural satellite},
  annotation = {titleTranslation: 小型自然卫星远距离逆行轨道解析表达式\\
abstractTranslation: 本研究获得了远距逆行轨道（DRO）的解析表达式。由于平面DRO是一种闭合轨道且可近似表示为椭圆轨道，本文解析计算了DRO的几何形状与周期。同时，确定了平面DRO的多种性质随轨道半径增大而发生突变的切换点。以火星-火卫二系统（Mars--Deimos system）为例进行案例分析，所提方法适用于限制性三体问题中Hill近似成立的情形。通过数值计算验证了该方法的有效性},
