  doi = {10.5139/IJASS.2010.11.3.206},
  urldate = {2025-11-27},
  abstract = {This paper proposes optimal control techniques for determining translational and rotational maneuvers that facilitate proximity operations and docking. Two candidate controllers that provide translational motion are compared. A state-dependent Riccati equation controller is formulated from nonlinear relative motion dynamics, and a linear quadratic tracking controller is formulated from linearized relative motion. A linear quadratic Gaussian controller using star trackers to provide quaternion measurements is designed for precision attitude maneuvering. The attitude maneuvers are evaluated for different final axis alignment geometries that depend on the approach distance. A six degrees-of-freedom simulation demonstrates that the controllers successfully perform proximity operations that meet the conditions for docking.},
  langid = {english},
  annotation = {titleTranslation: 近距离操作与对接的最优控制\\
abstractTranslation: 本文提出了用于确定平移和旋转机动的最优控制技术，以支持近距离操作与对接。比较了两种提供平移运动的候选控制器：一种基于非线性相对运动动力学构建的状态相关黎卡提方程控制器，以及一种基于线性化相对运动构建的线性二次型跟踪控制器。同时，设计了一种使用星敏感器提供四元数测量的线性二次型高斯控制器，用于实现精确的姿态机动。根据接近距离的不同，对不同最终轴线对准几何构型下的姿态机动进行了评估。六自由度仿真表明，这些控制器能够成功执行满足对接条件的近距离操作},
  file = {/home/ouyangjiahong/Zotero/storage/MZEN5MKP/Lee和Pernicka - 2010 - Optimal control for proximity operations and docking.pdf}
