  urldate = {2025-11-27},
  abstract = {The identification of trajectories that target a precise location and approach vector during planetary entry is sensitive to the quality of the startup arc supplied to iterative path planning and guidance algorithms. These sensitivities are especially evident when multi-body effects are significant, such as in Planet-to-Moon, Moon-to-Moon, Moon-to-Planet, Planet-to-Asteroid, or Moon-to-Asteroid transfers. They are also significant in interplanetary trajectories when maneuvers are scheduled within a region of space susceptible to multi-body effects. The present study considers precision entry targeting from the perspective of the multi-body problem.},
  langid = {english},
  annotation = {titleTranslation: 多体引力场中精确进入的动力学方法：色散流形\\
abstractTranslation: 在行星进入过程中，针对精确位置和接近矢量进行轨迹识别时，其效果高度依赖于提供给迭代路径规划与制导算法的启动弧段质量。当多体效应显著时，例如行星到月球、月球到月球、月球到行星、行星到小行星或月球到小行星转移，这些敏感性尤为突出。此外，当在易受多体效应影响的空间区域中安排机动时，星际轨迹中的敏感性同样显著。本研究从多体问题的视角探讨了精确进入目标定位。},
