  pages = {1283--1298},
  issn = {00945765},
  doi = {10.1016/j.actaastro.2008.05.016},
  urldate = {2025-11-27},
  abstract = {Upcoming National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) mission concepts include satellite arrays to facilitate imaging and identification of distant planets. These mission scenarios are diverse, including designs such as the terrestrial planet finder-occulter (TPF-O), where a monolithic telescope is aided by a single occulter spacecraft, and the micro-arcsecond Xray imaging mission (MAXIM), where as many as 16 spacecraft move together to form a space interferometer. Each design, however, requires precise reconfiguration and star tracking in potentially complex dynamic regimes. This paper explores control methods for satellite imaging array reconfiguration in multi-body systems. Specifically, optimal nonlinear control and geometric control methods are derived and compared to the more traditional linear quadratic regulators, as well as input state feedback linearization. These control strategies are implemented and evaluated for the TPF-O mission concept.},
  copyright = {https://www.elsevier.com/tdm/userlicense/1.0/},
  langid = {english},
  annotation = {titleTranslation: 多体引力场中航天器成像阵列的最优重构机动\\
abstractTranslation: 即将执行的美国国家航空航天局（NASA）任务概念包括卫星阵列，用以支持遥远行星的成像与识别。这些任务场景多种多样，例如``类地行星探测器-掩星器''（TPF-O）方案，其中单块式望远镜由一颗独立的掩星航天器辅助，以及``微角秒X射线成像任务''（MAXIM），多达16颗航天器协同运动，构成空间干涉仪。然而，每种设计都要求在潜在复杂的动态环境中实现精确的重构与恒星跟踪。本文探讨了多体系统中卫星成像阵列重构的控制方法。具体而言，推导了最优非线性控制与几何控制方法，并将其与传统的线性二次型调节器以及输入状态反馈线性化方法进行了比较。这些控制策略已在TPF-O任务概念中得以实现并评估。},
