  abstract = {Different and exciting exploration opportunities toward the Moon are opening in this decade. In particular, the major space agencies are putting a considerable effort in designing and studying a broad spectrum of missions that will bring back the humans on the Moon. During the evaluation of Lunar mission concepts, having a tool that can quickly assess the best communication and data-handling architecture given a set of satellites and a site of interest is mandatory. In this work, a novel parametric framework is presented and applied to the study of the expected connectivity of Lunar networks. The framework comprises bent-pipe, store-and-forward and store-carry-and-forward networking approaches, covering most common data management options. The methodology is designed to determine the best communication architecture given an arbitrary set of available satellites, ground stations, point of interest, and data volume. The proposed algorithm has been applied in a motivating case study of a networked mission devoted to observing lava tubes sites on the Moon surface. Results validate the approach which can identify the inflection points where different data handling techniques outperform each other.},
  langid = {english},
  annotation = {titleTranslation: 自主月球网络参数化数据处理评估框架\\
abstractTranslation: 在本十年中，多样而激动人心的月球探索机遇正逐步展开。尤为值得一提的是，各大主要航天机构正投入大量精力设计与研究一系列旨在将人类重新送回月球的使命方案。在评估月球任务概念时，拥有一套能够基于给定卫星集合和感兴趣地点快速评估最优通信与数据处理架构的工具至关重要。本文提出了一种新颖的参数化框架，并将其应用于月球网络预期连通性的研究。该框架涵盖了弯管、存储转发和存储携带转发等组网方式，囊括了最常见的数据管理选项。该方法旨在针对任意给定的可用卫星、地面站、兴趣点及数据量，确定最优通信架构。所提出的算法已应用于一个激励性的案例研究，该研究聚焦于一项旨在观测月球表面熔岩管地点的联网任务。结果验证了该方法的有效性，能够识别不同数据处理技术相互超越的拐点。},
