  urldate = {2025-11-27},
  abstract = {The mission design to a halo orbit around Lagrangian points from Earth involves, as a first step, the design of the halo orbit for the required size. This paper deals with the halo orbit design using Gradient and Non Gradient based optimization techniques. The conventional approach in literature uses a differential correction procedure to generate the preliminary design. The sensitivity of the governing dynamics requires a good initial guess and is provided by a higher order analytical solution. It is found that the differential correction procedure doesn't give the required out of plane amplitude in a single level scheme. This design needs refinement using some numerical continuation methods. In order to overcome this problem, a single level scheme based on Differential Evolution has been employed. The differential evolution based algorithm provides halo orbit design in a single level procedure. However, the computational time and effort for the basic differential evolution algorithm (Scheme 1) is found to be very large compared to the differential correction procedure. Two modified variants of differential evolution in terms of mutation strategies are employed. It is observed that the Scheme 2 performs better than all others in computational time and effort.},
  langid = {english},
  annotation = {titleTranslation: 基于梯度与非梯度优化技术的拉格朗日点晕轨道设计},
  file = {/home/ouyangjiahong/Zotero/storage/7AYBIWLS/Rithwik和Ramanan - 2018 - Halo orbit design around lagrangian points using gradient and non gradient based optimization techni.pdf}
