  pages = {2252--2273},
  doi = {10.1016/j.asr.2021.01.019},
  abstract = {A way to improve the accuracy of the three-body problem model is taking into account the eccentricity of primary attractors. Elliptic Restricted Three-Body Problem (ER3BP) is a model for studying spacecraft trajectory within the three-body problem such that the orbital eccentricity of primaries is reflected in it. As the principal cause of perturbation in the employed dynamical model, the primaries eccentricity changes the structure of orbits compared to the ideal Circular Restricted Three-Body Problem (CR3BP). It also changes the attitude behavior of a spacecraft revolving along periodic orbits in this regime. In this paper, the coupled orbit-attitude dynamics of a spacecraft in the ER3BP are exploited to find precise periodic solutions as the spacecraft is considered to be in planar orbits around Lagrangian points and Distant Retrograde Orbits (DRO). Periodic solutions are repetitious behaviors in which spacecraft whole dynamics are repeated periodically, these periodic behaviors are the main interest of this study because they are beneficial for future mission designs and allow delineation of the system's governing dynamics. Previous studies laid the foundation for spacecraft stability analysis or studying pitch motion of spacecraft in the ER3BP regime. While in this paper, at first, initial guesses for correction algorithms were derived through verified search methods, then correction algorithms were used to refine calculated orbit-attitude periodic behaviors. Periodic orbits and full periodic solutions are portrayed and compared to previous studies and simpler models. Natural periodic solutions are valuable information eventuate in the longer functional lifetime of spacecraft. Since the problem assumption considered in this paper is much closer to real mission conditions, these results may be the means to use natural bounded motions in the actual operational environment.},
  langid = {english},
  keywords = {Complex Environment,Correction algorithms,Coupled dynamics,ER3BP,Lagrangian points,Periodic solutions},
  annotation = {titleTranslation: 椭圆限制性三体问题中沿平面轨道的周期性姿态运动\\
abstractTranslation: 提高三体问题模型精度的一种方法是考虑主吸引体的偏心率。椭圆型限制性三体问题（ER3BP）是一种用于在三体问题框架内研究航天器轨道的模型，其中反映了主天体的轨道偏心率。作为所采用动力学模型中扰动的主要来源，主天体的偏心率改变了轨道结构，使其不同于理想的圆型限制性三体问题（CR3BP）。同时，它也改变了沿该机制中周期轨道运行的航天器的姿态行为。本文利用ER3BP中的耦合轨道-姿态动力学，在考虑航天器绕拉格朗日点及远距离逆行轨道（DRO）做平面运动的情况下，寻找精确的周期解。周期解是一种重复性行为，其中航天器的整体动力学呈周期性重复；这些周期行为是本研究的主要兴趣点，因为它们对未来任务设计有益，并有助于描述系统的支配动力学。以往的研究为航天器稳定性分析或ER3BP机制下俯仰运动的研究奠定了基础。而本文首先通过验证过的搜索方法推导出校正算法的初始猜测，随后利用校正算法对计算得到的轨道-姿态周期行为进行精化。文中展示了周期轨道与完整周期解，并与以往研究及更简单的模型进行了比较。自然周期解是具有价值的信息，可延长航天器的功能寿命。由于本文所考虑的问题假设更接近真实任务条件，这些结果可能成为在实际运行环境中利用自然束缚运动的手段}
}

