  urldate = {2025-11-27},
  abstract = {This paper addresses the computation of the required trajectory correction maneuvers for a halo orbit space mission to compensate for the launch velocity errors introduced by inaccuracies of the launch vehicle. By combining dynamical systems theory with optimal control techniques, we are able to provide a compelling portrait of the complex landscape of the trajectory design space. This approach enables automation of the analysis to perform parametric studies that simply were not available to mission designers a few years ago, such as how the magnitude of the errors and the timing of the rst trajectory correction maneuver a ects the correction V . The impetus for combining dynamical systems theory and optimal control in this problem arises from design issues for the Genesis Discovery Mission being developed for NASA by the Jet Propulsion Laboratory. ? 2002 Elsevier Science Ltd. All rights reserved.},
  copyright = {https://www.elsevier.com/tdm/userlicense/1.0/},
  langid = {english},
  annotation = {titleTranslation: 基于最优控制的晕轨道任务修正机动\\
abstractTranslation: 本文研究了为补偿运载火箭不精确性所引入的发射速度误差，在晕轨道空间任务中所需的轨迹修正机动计算。通过将动力系统理论与最优控制技术相结合，我们得以描绘出轨迹设计空间中复杂景观的引人入胜的图景。该方法实现了分析自动化，能够进行几年前任务设计者根本无法实现的参数研究，例如误差大小和首次轨迹修正机动时机如何影响修正速度增量。在该问题中结合动力系统理论与最优控制的动力来自美国宇航局喷气推进实验室正在开发的Genesis Discovery Mission的设计问题。\copyright{} 2002 Elsevier Science Ltd. 保留所有权利},
